   "evidence": "TruncatedExpansion.lean:41 `variable {\ud835\udd5c E : Type*} [NormedField \ud835\udd5c] ...`; :48 `theorem isBigO_pow_pow {m n : \u2115} (h : m \u2264 n) : (fun x : \ud835\udd5c => x ^ n) =O[\ud835\udcdd 0] fun x => x ^ m`. The TauCeti lemma it is derived from needs only `[SeminormedAddCommGroup E]` (upstream/TauCeti/TauCeti/Analysis/Asymptotics/Lemmas.lean:55), and `NormedDivisionRing.toNormedRing` / `NormedDivisionRing.toNormMulClass` (Mathlib/Analysis/Normed/Field/Basic.lean:52,58) supply the norm structure and `norm_pow` the proof uses.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/Analysis/Asymptotics/TruncatedExpansion.lean",
   "fix": "Put it in its own section with `variable {\ud835\udd5c : Type*} [NormedDivisionRing \ud835\udd5c]` (the rest of the file needs `NormedField` only for `NormedSpace \ud835\udd5c E`). At that class it is also provable from Mathlib alone: `h.eq_or_lt.elim (\u00b7 \u25b8 isBigO_refl _ _) fun h => (isLittleO_pow_pow h).isBigO`.",
   "issue": "`Asymptotics.isBigO_pow_pow` inherits `[NormedField \ud835\udd5c]` from the file-wide `variable` block (line 41), but its Mathlib sibling \u2014 which its own docstring cites \u2014 is `Asymptotics.isLittleO_pow_pow` at `[NormedDivisionRing \ud835\udd5c]` (upstream/mathlib/Mathlib/Analysis/Asymptotics/Lemmas.lean:583, section variable at line 39). Nothing in the statement or proof needs commutativity, and the lemma is in an upstream namespace, so it carries the stronger class into PhyslibAlpha.",
